          %h1#validity Validity
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#validity_in_modal_logic"} Validity in modal logic
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            %strong valid
            relative to a specified logic if its form in that logic is such that whenever the premises are true then the conclusion must be true.
          %p
            A logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formula"} formula
            is said to be valid if it true under every
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpretation"} interpretation
          %h2#validity_in_modal_logic Validity in modal logic
          %p
            To judge whether a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+logic"} modal logic
            gives a good encoding of the properties of a particular relational structure, we need to put aside the valuations and to concentrate on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+%28modal+logic%29"} frames
            %strong valid
            on a frame
            %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔉
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
            if it is true at every state in every model that can be built from
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔉
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  A formula
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  is said to be
                  %em valid at a state
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
                  is a frame
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔉
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}= (W,R_1,\ldots, R_n)
                  (notation
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔉
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F},w \models \phi
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  is true at
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
                  in every model
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔉
                          %mo ,
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M} = (\mathfrak{F},V)
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔉
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
              %li
                %p
                  A formula,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  %em valid in a frame
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔉
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
                  (notation
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔉
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}\models \phi
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔉
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔽
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
                  is a class of frames (all of the same relational signature), then we say
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  is
                  %em
                    valid in
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔽
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
                  (notation
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}\models \phi
                  if
                  %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔉
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}\models \phi
                  for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔉
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝔽
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}\in \mathbb{F}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong valid
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \models\phi
          %p
            Fixing a given set
            %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            of atomic formulae and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+%28in+logic%29"} relational signature
            that we are considering:
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The set of formulae that are valid on a class,
              %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{F}
              , of frames of that signature forms a logic.
          %p (We restrict to Kripke frames (i.e. to binary relations) for simplicity of exposition, and refer to the sources, such as Blackburn et al, for a fuller discussion.)
          %p
            We denote the logic thus specified by
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_1e104322a286565f022d193487036a434d8ce1b9_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_\mathbf{F}
          %h2#references References
